    <h1>France VPN with No Browsing Logs</h1>
    <p class="article-intro">Most VPNs display "no logs" without explaining what that means. Here's what VulcainVPN actually logs, what it doesn't, and why — in full transparency.</p>

    <h2>What "No Browsing Logs" Actually Means</h2>
    <p>There are two categories of data a VPN could theoretically record:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Activity logs</strong> — sites you visit, what you download, DNS queries, browsing history. This is what advertisers, governments, and hackers are after.</li>
      <li><strong>Connection metadata</strong> — your IP, connection time, approximate location. These are minimal technical data points.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>VulcainVPN <strong>never collects activity logs</strong>. What you do online is completely private and never recorded.</p>

    <h2>What We Do Log (And Why)</h2>
    <p>To be honest: we temporarily collect minimal connection metadata. This is necessary for two concrete reasons:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Enforcing the 3-device limit</strong> — each subscription allows 3 simultaneous connections. Without monitoring active connections, we can't enforce this.</li>
      <li><strong>Detecting account theft</strong> — if your account is used in France and Asia simultaneously, that's likely a stolen password. We detect this and block the suspicious connection.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="article-highlight">
      <h3>What We Temporarily Collect</h3>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> Your IP address — to identify the device</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> Connection timestamp — for the device limit</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> Approximate location (city/country) — to detect account theft</p>
      <p><span class="checkmark">➤</span> Anonymous identifier — a random code, not your email</p>
      <br>
      <p><strong>Retention period: 24-48 hours maximum, then automatic deletion.</strong></p>
    </div>

    <h2>Why This Differs from Absolute "No Logs"</h2>
    <p>A VPN claiming absolute "no logs" is either lying or unable to detect abuse. We prefer transparency: we collect the minimum necessary, delete it quickly, and never look at what you do online.</p>
    <p>Our full policy is published and readable: <a href="<%= logging_path %>">Logging Policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>France-Based Server, GDPR</h2>
    <p>Our servers are hosted in France. Data is processed under French jurisdiction and GDPR protection. We never transfer your data to third countries.</p>

    <div class="article-cta">
